/target
Cargo.lock
*.wasm.map
.DS_Store

# credentials never belong in the repo
.env
*.token
acw_token*

# scratch probes: a subagent auditing this repo writes throwaway examples to check a claim, and
# they must never reach a commit. Named so they cannot be confused with the real probe examples
# (certify_probe, encoding_probe, ...) which are checked in on purpose.
zz_*
tmp_*
**/audit_*.rs
**/*_audit_*.rs
**/*_probe_*.rs
**/*_refute*.rs

# npm's install tree for the browser tests. `npm install` recreates it from package-lock.json, and
# committing it once put 181 files and 15 MB into both the repository and the published crate.
# No trailing slash. `node_modules/` matches a DIRECTORY, and a symlink to one is not a directory --
# which is how a symlink pointing at an absolute path on one machine got committed, survived review,
# and broke `cargo publish` at the next release. Both forms, so neither shape gets through.
node_modules
node_modules/

# The Python build tree and the staged native library. build-python-wheel.sh copies the cdylib into
# the package to build a wheel and removes it afterwards; if a build is interrupted it must not be
# committed, because a checkout carrying a stale binary behaves differently from a fresh clone.
python/build/
python/dist/
python/*.egg-info/
python/ferrotherm/*.so
python/ferrotherm/*.dylib
python/ferrotherm/*.dll

# Zig's build cache and output. `zig build` creates these beside build.zig, and they arrived the
# moment that file did: 47 MB of object files, into both the repository and the published crate.
.zig-cache/
zig-out/

# Julia manifests. A Manifest.toml pins resolved dependency versions and belongs to an APPLICATION,
# not to a package: shipping one from a package means every consumer inherits whatever was resolved
# on the author's machine. A stale one here listed no LazyArtifacts and failed CI with
# "direct dependency, but does not appear in the manifest".
julia/*/Manifest.toml
